# Line endings.
#
# The default for authored files: git stores LF and checks out whatever suits
# the platform.
* text=auto

# --- but not for anything we did not write. --------------------------------
#
# The official NCHS/CMS releases are stored verbatim. They are not consistent
# with each other -- `icd10cm_order_2027.txt` ships CRLF while the code files
# and every XML ship LF -- and normalising them would mean the file checked
# out of this repo is not the file CMS published. `-text` tells git to leave
# every byte alone in both directions.
#
# This is not fussiness. A CRLF that survives into a data file welds a stray
# \r onto the last column of every row, which then becomes part of a code.
# See the note on `rows()` and `write_text()` in CLAUDE.md.
"Table and Index/*"    -text
"Code Descriptions/*"  -text
Guidelines/*           -text

# The two single-file builds carry a gzipped, base64-encoded payload of the
# whole data set. They must come back byte-for-byte identical to what
# `build/bundle.py` and `build/bundle2.py` wrote.
icd10cm-notes-explorer.html   -text
icd10-coder-workbench.html    -text

# Generated data is not committed (see .gitignore), but if it ever is, it is
# tab-separated and must not be touched either.
*.tsv   -text

# Language hints, so GitHub reports the repo as what it is rather than as a
# pile of XML.
*.xml       linguist-vendored
*.xsd       linguist-vendored
*.txt       linguist-vendored
*.html      linguist-detectable
